See https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file for more about ignoring files.

-- SCM & Development Tools --

Ignore git directory (Reduces build context significantly).

!/.git/
/.gitignore

Ignore CI service files.

/.github

Ignore development files (VS Code, DevContainers, etc).

/.devcontainer
/.vscode

-- Dependencies --

Ignore bundler config.

/.bundle
/vendor/bundle

-- Environment & Secrets --

Ignore all environment files (except templates).

/.env*
!/.env*.erb

Ignore all default key files.

/config/master.key
/config/credentials/*.key

-- Rails Runtime & Artifacts --

Ignore all logfiles and tempfiles.

/log/*
/tmp/*
!/log/.keep
!/tmp/.keep

Ignore pidfiles, but keep the directory.

/tmp/pids/*
!/tmp/pids/.keep

Ignore storage (uploaded files in development and any SQLite databases).

/storage/*
!/storage/.keep
/tmp/storage/*
!/tmp/storage/.keep

-- Assets --

Ignore assets (Node modules and compiled assets).

/node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/
/app/assets/builds/*
!/app/assets/builds/.keep
/public/assets

-- Docker Metadata --

Ignore Docker-related files to prevent cache invalidation.

/.dockerignore
/Dockerfile*
/docker-compose*
